title the fold writes its own trail -- the loom takes back the three facts it already held, and the two roster passes hand back four more reds on the way
prompt The HUSH seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves, claim-as-override when my lane's queue is empty. My own last recommend and the card both named the door: the fold-trail loom, after the lane-safe choirs.
think LISTAGENTS FIRST -- none reachable, and the process listing agreed: one eleven-day-old jailed claude in ~/grain and nothing else. No peer roster pass, no worktree hand, so no file of mine crossed anyone.
think ROTA ROW 1 BY N=3861 MOD 5 -- Air, Saturn, law and boundary, the row whose sense is touch: you cannot touch a thing's middle, only where it ends. Its question read as this round's own instruction. The fence I walked was the one inside the fold tool: which facts a tool may write and which belong to a hand. The tool's header drew that line at the whole recital row, and the line was in the wrong place -- it sorts the rows, it reads each row's status marker, and it is handed the shelf, so two of the three facts it called authorial were its own readings.
think THE CARD NAMED TWO DOORS AND I TOOK THE SECOND FIRST. Lane-safe choirs (drey 17, acme_dx 11) measure coverage; the fold-trail loom closes a class that had fired TWICE in one day with its ratchet sitting exactly at its ceiling -- unrecorded_shelves 62 against a ceiling of 62, so the next untrailed fold reds a rostered guard for every body in the fleet. Crux-first took the loom.
think THE COLD PASS PREEMPTED BOTH: 104 guards, 102 green, 2 red, and only ONE of them was the known gate. shell_dialect read gated_stat_c_sites=1 against a ceiling of 0. The site was tools/f/fleet_rearm.sh, landed hours earlier the same day, writing its own mtime_of() as `stat -f %m ... || stat -c %Y ...` -- BSD-first, which on this GNU host asks for the filesystem holding a file named %m, prints a block report, and only then falls through. REDS %260's exact trap, in the family the guard had promoted to gated that same day.
think READING THE HELPER'S OTHER CALLERS FOUND THE SECOND, WHICH NOTHING WAS WATCHING. tools/ad/ad_walk_sample.sh sourced ../fixtures/shell_portable.sh -- the home before the 20260828 letter fold -- so the script died on its source line and printed nothing. A source path is not a link any scan reads, so no guard could have said so. One root under both: a shared answer is worth exactly its reach.
think THE LOOM, DRAWN SO THE TOOL STILL REFUSES TO INVENT MEANING. `--why` is required and carries the one authorial part; the tool writes the rest. Runs of three or more consecutive rows compress to a range the way every standing recital row reads, and a run of two stays two items. The status word comes from the markers the row loop already parsed -- and a row carrying no bold marker drops the clause rather than inferring one, which is the honest answer rather than the convenient one.
obs THE PROOF RAN IN /tmp WHILE THE COLD PASS OWNED THE TREE. The runner's digest now reads content, so any edit during a 40-minute pass closes it tree_moved. So the whole loom was drafted, penned and proven outside the repository -- 62 behaviours green before one byte of the tree moved -- and copied in when the pass closed. Holding still cost nothing this round because the work went somewhere else.
obs THE CLAUSE BOUND IS MEASURED RATHER THAN CHOSEN. The longest clause standing on the recital measures 925 bytes, so MAX_WHY is 1,024 -- the next power of two above every real case, proven from both sides in the pen: 1,024 welcomed, 1,025 refused. why_non_ascii catches a newline by the same test, because the row is ONE line and the capacity scan greps it whole.
obs ITS FIRST USE IN THE FIELD WAS THE FOLD THAT MADE ROOM FOR ITS OWN ROW. The pin stood at 784 bytes of headroom with rows_that_fit=0, so booking anything meant folding first: %377-%380 onto their shelf, trail line written by the tool, unrecorded_shelves unchanged at 62 -- the first fold in this ledger's history that could not forget its own trail.
obs FETCH-BEFORE-BOOK EARNED ITS PLACE AGAIN. next_free read 381 and the same fetch showed xy four commits ahead, two of them touching construction/. Stashed, fast-forwarded, popped clean, then re-read the spine: still 381. Booked %381 and %382, advanced the headline 380 to 382 with the monotone witness rather than by hand -- %378's own lesson, one row after it folded.
obs THE HOT PASS IS WHERE THIS LAP EARNED ITS SECOND HALF: 104 run, 98 green, SIX red, and only one of them was the gate. readme_reach found FOURTEEN day-shelf index rows linking their log by bare filename from one directory up -- four hands in one evening, after I repaired eleven of the same shape the lap before -- and reds_fold cascaded off the same scan. witness_reach read 1,094 unreached against a ceiling of 1,093 and unheard_guard rose with it, both because Sound's nesting law landed with its own witness and no clock in the four commits I had just fast-forwarded over. remember_git_nib reds until the commit exists. Repaired: fourteen rows carry their 20260830/ room, and glow_preset_offset joins the roster at tier lap, 31s on metal and GREEN before its row was written -- the guard's own refusal names that answer rather than a raised ceiling.
obs THE INDEX-ROW CLASS IS BOOKED RATHER THAN CLOSED (%383), because the repair rate and the writing rate are the same number. Both guards that catch it run only inside a 45-minute pass, so every hand writes its row, passes a roster, and learns about the row an hour later from somebody else's repair. The remainder is one booked lap: a commit-time reading of the touched day shelf's own links, in tools/hooks/pre-commit beside the pages it already regenerates.
obs %374'S COST WAS PAID IN FULL BY THIS LAP, TWICE. Both passes closed guard_red at gates, so no receipt was written, so --scoped was unreachable and each re-verify had to be either the whole 45-minute roster again or a named set. I took the named set for the repair: the thirteen guards the scope map shows watching session-logs/ and construction/, plus tracked_link, every one green on metal. That is the honest shape and it is also the exact evidence the receipt-chain question wants: this pier can never earn the cheaper pass while two reds sit at gates Keaton named.
obs THE PEER'S FILE WAS LANDED, NEVER IN FLIGHT. fleet_rearm.sh was committed hours before I touched it and no peer process was running; the charter forbids touching in-flight work rather than a peer's landed file, and the guard it reds is rostered for every body. Named here rather than assumed.
loom roster=cold guards_run=104 green=102 red=2 tree_moved=no
loom roster=hot guards_run=104 green=98 red=6 tree_moved=no wall_min=48
loom reverify guards=14 green=14 red=0 scope=session-logs+construction
loom glow_preset_offset wall_s=31 verdict=green tier=lap
loom control=reds_fold behaviours=62 elder=27 added=35 fail=0
loom pin_before_bytes=23792 headroom_before=784 pin_after_bytes=22377 headroom_after=2199
loom unrecorded_shelves=62 ceiling=62 phantom=0
loom qa cards=5 grade=A composite=94 setting=meter service=75
file tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold.sh the loom writes the recital row; --why required, six new refusals before a byte moves
file tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold_control.sh thirty-five behaviours on real pins in a pen, the clause bound both ways
file tools/r/reds_fold_witness.rish the count moves 27 to 62 and the GREEN line names what it now proves
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md the header says who writes these rows now; the loom's first line beneath it
file construction/archive/REDS-what-a-meter-actually-reads-rows-377-380.md four instruments and what each was actually reading
file construction/REDS.md %381 and %382 CLOSED, %383 BOOKED; the headline advanced by measurement, three times
file tools/f/fleet_rearm.sh the mtime question reaches the tree's one answer instead of a second copy
file tools/ad/ad_walk_sample.sh the helper's letter-room home, so the script runs again
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260830.md fourteen rows take their day room, and this lap's own row
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri glow_preset_offset joins at tier lap, with the reading that wanted it
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Now line, the doors, this lap's roster reading, the nib
recommend keep-going -- THE LOOM STANDS AND ITS FIRST FOLD PROVED IT (and the hot pass then handed back four more reds, three of them repaired here), and the dialect red that preempted this lap is closed at the source rather than at the ceiling. MINE NEXT, unchanged from my last two recommends: the lane-safe choirs, drey 17 and acme_dx 11, measured on metal and rostered at the tier their wall time earns -- that is %360's remainder in the one lane nobody else holds. YOUR GATES ARE WHERE THEY WERE: rule_twin at %7, drift 38 over 36 and still growing two-way; %374's receipt-chain question stays yours.
